build the core picker's art only for a gba cart

Only a GBA cart opens the core picker (App::open_core_picker returns for
anything else), but sync_core_picker asked FaceBuilder for its lid, board
and interior on every change of highlight, whatever the cart. Traced on the
handheld on the NES shelf, 2026-10-31: every step along it uploaded a 1x1,
a 360x212 and a 308x347 texture inside the frame, and the builder thread
behind them was a third busy thread on two cores beside the cart-face
workers -- which on the same trace were still making compose wait 36-100 ms
when moving between shelves.

The request is now made only for a GBA cart. The art is drawn by the
picker and nothing else, so nothing on screen changes; a GBA cart builds
exactly as it did.

Tested on the host: slot's tests fail in the same places with and without
it. Played on the Flip with 0036 and 0037 (2026-10-31).

Applies on top of 0034, upstream 91499a9.

diff --git a/crates/slot/src/frontend.rs b/crates/slot/src/frontend.rs
index 42fa477..9ec6874 100644
--- a/crates/slot/src/frontend.rs
+++ b/crates/slot/src/frontend.rs
@@ -1254,9 +1254,15 @@ fn sync_core_picker(
 ) {
     let highlighted = app.selected_stem().map(str::to_string);
     if highlighted.is_some() && *asked != highlighted {
+        // Only a GBA cart opens the picker (`App::open_core_picker`). Built for
+        // every cart, each step along an NES or Game Boy shelf cost a lid, a
+        // board and an interior on a thread contending with the cart-face
+        // workers for two cores, and three uploads inside the frame, for art
+        // that is never drawn.
         if let Some(cart) = app
             .carts()
             .find(|c| highlighted.as_deref() == Some(c.stem.as_str()))
+            .filter(|c| c.platform == Console::Gba)
         {
             builder.request(cart.clone());
         }
